# PTCS Dynamic renderer owner UX fixes

## Pre-work plan

- Background: Daedalus reported that an outlined black Fill marker is present in DOM/hit-testing but invisible on a dark plot, data-window tokens are constrained to a fixed scrolling strip, cursor event rows conflate absent events with unavailable capability, and trace controls remain row-scoped.
- Goal: deliver the smallest owner-side contract/renderer/test slice that restores visible marker contrast and correct generic presentation semantics without moving SPAA projection logic into PTCS Dynamic.
- Invariants: preserve semantic marker color and overview 1px stripe behavior; do not mutate Daedalus scenario/projection data; no JavaScript implementation; keep existing exact package graph.
- Scope: Dynamic Contracts/Renderer/Interactive.Client and focused F# verifiers only where required.
- Acceptance: dark-surface outline marker has a contrast under-stroke and visible-pixel regression; data window wraps with auto height and no internal scroll; cursor events distinguish None from Unavailable; any per-trace contract change has focused tests and explicit owner boundary.
- Risk: per-trace removal can alter durable workspace intent; do not implement it until existing contracts and scenario-generation semantics are verified.
- Stop condition: focused builds/tests and browser gate pass, package/dependency graph is verified, docs/log are updated, commit/push completes, or a genuine upstream contract blocker is reported to Daedalus.

